-- title:
--   Descent of the rigid chart to the fixed field K₀ at q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`.
--
--   **Data.** A prime $q$ subject to $q=3$ (`hq3`); a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$; a valuation subring $A\subset\bar{\mathbb Q}$ which lies over $q$ in the sense of [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`). Write $\kappa=\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ and $F_\kappa=\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC }\kappa\,M'$, the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa$-Laurent series generated by the $j$-series `jqModC` and its $M'$-fold expansion `jqNModC`. A finite set $W$ of places of $F_\kappa$ (a place being a proper valuation subring containing the base field and being a principal ideal ring) is assumed by `hW` to consist exactly of the places in `ssPlaces q M' κ`, those satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace` for $q$ and $M'$; $s\in W$ is a distinguished such place. By `hle`, the base change $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar }M'$ to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$ is contained in $\mathtt{fieldBar }q\,M'$, the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $H=\mathtt{levelH }q\,M'$ (the kernel of the unit-group reduction `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`). Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar }M'$ relative to $A$ with values in $F_\kappa$: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` together with a surjective residue map onto $F_\kappa$ with kernel the maximal ideal, a degree-preserving map on places, and the usual compatibilities with $A$ on constants. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series lies in $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar }M'$, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A\to\kappa$.
--
--   **Small constants.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ with $\pi_0\in A$ (`hπ`). Put $A_0=A\cap k_0$, formally `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`. It is assumed that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$ (`hunif`), that $A_0$ is henselian local (`hhens`), that its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary parameters.** A prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖtA`, `hϖt`); an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b=\bot$ (`hKb`) and a valuation subring $A_b\subset K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$ (`hAb`), with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi_b\neq 0$ (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`); a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi\in k_0$ (`hξ`); and the tameness hypothesis `htame` that $\ell_g-1$ is a unit of $A_0$.
--
--   **Level and chart.** $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is, by `hH₁`, the intersection of $\mathtt{levelH }q\,M'$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$ (using $\ell_g\mid M'\mid q^2M'$). The field $K_\ell$ is an intermediate field of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}(k_0)/k_0$ equal, by `hKℓ`, to the base change $\mathtt{laurentBaseChange }k_0\,(\mathtt{xHFunctionField }(q^2M')\,H_1)$; it carries the evident $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$. The element $j_\ell\in K_\ell$ is non-zero and equals, by `hjℓ`, the image $\mathtt{coeffEmb }k_0\,\mathtt{jq}$ of the rational $j$-series. Let $C=\mathtt{chartAlgFin }A_0\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$ be the finite-$j$ chart, i.e. the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$. Further data: $\varpi_t'\in A_0$ with $\varpi_t'=\varpi_t$ (`hϖt'`); a maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ (`hy`) containing $\pi_0$ (`hϖy`); subalgebra $B_t\subseteq K_\ell$ over $A_0$ and valuation subring $W_t\subseteq K_\ell$ with $B_t\subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`); naturals $n,m$; $\gamma_0\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$; a $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$; an element $\zeta_c$ of the $\pi_0$-adic completion of $A_0$; the hypothesis `hjK` that $\mathtt{jqNModC }k_0\,q$ — the series obtained from the $j$-series by the $q$-fold expansion operator `qExpand` — lies in $K_\ell$; an element $a_0\in A_0$; and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$.
--
--   For $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ and an automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$, the predicate $\mathtt{IsLevelAutAt }k_0\,q\,\xi\,q\,(q^2M')\,H_1\,\gamma\,K_\ell\,\tau$ says that $\tau$ realises the slash action of the matrix $\mathtt{conjElemN }q\,\gamma$ on $q$-expansions: for all weights, all modular forms $f,g$ of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, all $x\in K_\ell$ equal to the corresponding quotient of series, and every embedding $\iota$ of $k_0$ into $\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\mathtt{conjElemN }q\,\gamma$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k\mathtt{conjElemN }q\,\gamma$. Below, 'a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$' means an automorphism $\tau$ with this property for $\gamma^{-1}$.
--
--   **Hypotheses on the point $y$.** `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from $C$ to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ lies in $\mathtt{ssJSet }q\,\Omega$, the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves are supersingular (every $q$-torsion point vanishes). `hover`: $y$ lies over $s$, in the sense that for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ over $\mathbb Q$ whose image lies in `R₀.integers`, which is regular at every place of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar }M'$ where the $j$-series is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathtt{evalAt}$ of that residue, the chart element $\mathtt{coeffEmb }k_0\,g$ minus $c$ lies in $y$. `hOrbit`: every maximal ideal $y'$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ which satisfies the same 'lying over $s$' condition is matched with $y$ by some level automorphism: there are $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and inducing a bijection between $y$ and $y'$. `hjC` and `ha₀y` state that $\mathtt{jqNModC }k_0\,q$ lies in $C$ and that its difference with $a_0$ lies in $y$.
--
--   **The rigid chart.** The hypothesis `hS1` (fourteen clauses, summarised here) asserts: $C\subseteq B_t$; $K_\ell$ is the field of fractions of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$; $B_t/(\pi_0)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t\cap k_0=A_0$; the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is generated by $\pi_0$; $W_t$ is a discrete valuation ring; $y$ is the contraction to $C$ of the maximal ideal of $W_t$; $W_t$ is the localisation of $B_t$ outside that maximal ideal; for every $\mathtt{GaloisField }q\,2$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A_0$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B_t$ onto $\mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing }q$ of that residue field whose vanishing locus is the maximal ideal of $W_t$, compatible with reduction of constants, and equivariant for level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) at a unit $c$ with $(\mathtt{redQ }q\,\gamma,c)\in\mathtt{hSubgroup }q$, with $c\neq 1$ for non-trivial $\tau$ coming from $\Gamma(q)$ and with the scalar $c$ alone also realised by a further level automorphism; $B_t$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is carried into the maximal ideal of $W_t$ by some level automorphism attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; and an element of $B_t$ all of whose level translates lie in the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   **Numerology and deck data.** $1\le n$ (`hn1`), $n\mid q+1$ (`hnq`), and $n=2\,\mathtt{placeWidthChar }q\,M'\,s$ (`hn`), the latter being `jWidthChar` of $s.\mathtt{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen})$ divided by `placeRamificationJ`; $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma_0\in\Gamma_0(M')$; $\tau_0$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ (`hτ₀`) preserving $W_t$ (`hτ₀W`); $1\le m$ and $\pi_0^m=\varpi_t'$ times a unit of $A_0$ (`hm1`, `hm`); $\zeta_c^n=1$ and $\zeta_c^k-1$ is a unit for $0<k<n$ (`hζc`, `hζcprim`).
--
--   **Ends and crossing data.** The hypothesis `hR7` (twelve clauses, summarised here) asserts: $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B_t$ pointwise while $\tau_0^k$ moves some element of $B_t$ for $0<k<n$; every level automorphism attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with some power $\tau_0^k$, $k<n$; `ends` has exactly $q+1$ elements; level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ permute `ends`, act transitively on it, and $\tau_0$ preserves every end; distinct ends are separated by an element which is a unit in one and not in the other; there is a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_c$, stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, contained in every end and with every end a localisation of it; an end mapped into $W_t$ by a level automorphism forces that automorphism to preserve $W_t$; each end $O$ is contained in $W_t$, is local and noetherian, contains $C$, satisfies $O\cap k_0=A_0$ and has every element at finite distance from a constant, and carries crossing data: elements $c_x,c_y$ with $c_xc_y=\pi_0^m$ times a unit, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}$ over the $\pi_0$-adic completion of $A_0$ at parameter $\pi_0^m$ carrying constants to `const` and $c_x,c_y$ to unit multiples of $U$ and $V$, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, with $\mathtt{jqNModC }k_0\,q-a_0$ going to a unit times $V^e$ for some $e\ge1$, with $\tau_0$ intertwined through $\iota$ by an automorphism $\theta_0$ of the crossing model satisfying $\theta_0U\equiv\zeta_cU$ and $\theta_0V\equiv\zeta_c^{-1}V$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal, together with a discrete valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ adapted to $O$ (containing $O$ and $C$, with $W_x\cap k_0=A_0$, uniformiser $\pi_0$, a non-degeneracy clause for a parameter $t$ and for $\mathtt{jqNModC }k_0\,q$ against polynomials over $A_0$, detecting $y$ on $C$, and singling out $O$ among the ends), and a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_x\subseteq B_t\cap O$, stable under level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, consisting of functions regular wherever $j_\ell$ is, with $O$ its localisation and containing an element escaping all valuation subrings at which $j_\ell$ stays integral; finally, any valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with $V\cap k_0=A_0$ containing $C$ and detecting $y$ either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends. The hypothesis `hR9` provides an element of $B_t$ lying in no valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with $V\cap k_0=A_0$, with $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, at which $j_\ell$ satisfies no monic integral congruence; `hR10` provides, for every maximal ideal $y''$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ not matched with $y$ by any level automorphism attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, an element of $B_t$ escaping every valuation subring containing $C$ which detects the corresponding translate of $y''$.
--
--   **Naming block.** $G$ is the subgroup of $k_0$-automorphisms of $K_\ell$ generated by the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`); $K_0=K_\ell^G$ is the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`); $B_0$ is an $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ whose elements are exactly the $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$ (`hB₀`); and $W_0'$ is a valuation subring of $K_0$ whose elements are exactly those of $K_0$ lying in $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** The following hold.
--
--   (1) For $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $K_0$ lies in $W_0'$.
--
--   (2) $W_0'$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (3) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0'$ and the maximal ideal of $W_0'$ is generated by it.
--
--   (4) For every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ over $\mathbb Q$ such that its image in $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar }M'$ lies in `R₀.integers`, such that $\operatorname{ord}_P(g)\ge0$ at every place $P$ of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar }M'$ with $\operatorname{ord}_P(\mathtt{jq})\ge0$, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$: whenever $\mathtt{coeffEmb }k_0\,g$ lies in $K_\ell$, it lies in $K_0$, the corresponding element of $K_0$ lies in $W_0'$, and for every $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathtt{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of that element with the image of $c$ lies in $W_0'$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0'$.
--
--   (5) For every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, and every $f\in K_\ell$ with both $f\in K_0$ and $\tau f\in K_0$: $f$ lies in $W_0'$ if and only if $\tau f$ does.
--
--   (6) Moreover, for the invariant algebra $B_0$:
--
--   (a) for every $a\in A_0$, the image of $a$ in $B_0$ is, in $K_\ell$, the image of $a$ under $k_0\to K_\ell$;
--
--   (b) $B_0\subseteq K_0$;
--
--   (c) every $f\in K_0$ can be written as a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_0$ and $h\neq0$;
--
--   (d) $B_0$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$;
--
--   (e) $B_0/(\pi_0)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (f) every element of $B_0$ lies in $K_0$ and in $W_0'$;
--
--   (g) the image of $\pi_0$ in $B_0$ is a prime element;
--
--   (h) an element $f\in K_0$ lies in $W_0'$ precisely when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_0$ and $\pi_0\nmid h$ in $B_0$; that is, $W_0'$ is the localisation of $B_0$ at $(\pi_0)$;
--
--   (i) $\mathtt{coeffEmb }k_0\,\mathtt{jq}$, whenever it lies in $K_\ell$, lies in $B_0$;
--
--   (j) $B_0$ is stable under every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (k) for every $\mathtt{GaloisField }q\,2$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ and every proof that $\mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing }q\,\kappa$ is a domain, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathtt{GaloisField }q\,2$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B_0$ to $\mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.quotField }q\,\kappa\,C_s$ — the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field $\operatorname{Frac}(\mathtt{CoordRing }q\,\kappa)$ of the subgroup generated by the automorphisms $\mathtt{hFunctionFieldAction }q\,\kappa$ at $(1,\zeta)$ for $\zeta\in C_s$ — such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ is $2\,\mathtt{placeWidthChar }q\,M'\,s$; the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$; $\rho$ sends the image of $a\in A_0$ to the image of the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; every element of the target is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h\in B_0$ and $\rho(h)\neq0$; an element of the target lies in the range of $\rho$ exactly when its image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of $\mathtt{CoordRing }q\,\kappa$; and, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, every witness that $(\mathtt{redQ }q\,\gamma,1)\in\mathtt{hSubgroup }q$, and every $f\in B_0$ with $\tau f\in B_0$, the image of $\rho(\tau f)$ in the Drinfeld function field is obtained from that of $\rho(f)$ by $\mathtt{hFunctionFieldAction }q\,\kappa$ at that element of $\mathtt{hSubgroup }q$.
--
--   This is the invariant-theoretic descent step in the analysis of the supersingular points of the modular curve at the prime $q=3$, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-framed setting: starting from a rigid chart $(B_t,W_t)$ over the auxiliary level $H_1$ together with its ends and crossing data, it produces on the fixed field $K_0$ of the level group a formally smooth, finitely presented model $B_0$ whose localisation at $\pi_0$ is a discrete valuation ring $W_0'$ compatible with $A$ on constants, and identifies the special fibre of $B_0$ with a subfield of the Drinfeld function field cut out by a group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of order twice the width of the place $s$. It is used by the level-descent statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
